# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Every variable here is OPTIONAL — with none of them set the
# app runs exactly as it always has: fully client-side, all state in localStorage.

# --- Supabase (multi-device sync) ---------------------------------------------------------
# Without these two the app is local-only: no account, no network, no sync.
# With them, every cook signs up, joins a restaurant with a 6-character code, and the whole
# AppState syncs in real time. See "Two modes, same app" in CLAUDE.md.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here

# --- Google Gemini (AI recipe scanning) ---------------------------------------------------
# Enables "photograph a recipe → structured draft" in the Recipes screen. Without it that
# screen falls back to on-device OCR only (tesseract.js), which is what it did before.
#
# NOTE THE MISSING VITE_ PREFIX, and do not add one. Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into
# the JavaScript the browser downloads, which would make the key public on a deployed site.
# This one is read only by the server (api/scan-recipe.ts) and never reaches the browser.
#
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey, then set it in BOTH places:
#   - here in .env.local, for `npm run dev`
#   - in Vercel → Project Settings → Environment Variables, for the deployed site
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
